  "title": "Colours",
  "level": "preschool",
  "category": "Vocabulary",
  "introduction": "Learn about colours through simple examples and practice.",
  "definition": "Colours describe how things look. The traditional seven rainbow colours are red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet. We also use everyday colour names such as pink, brown, black, white and grey.",
  "rules": [
    "Rainbow order: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet.",
    "Look at objects around you and name their colours.",
    "Say: The strawberry is red.",
    "Say: The carrot is orange.",
    "Say: The lemon is yellow.",
    "Say: The leaf is green.",
    "Say: The butterfly is blue.",
    "Say: The grapes are purple.",
    "Say: The cloud is grey.",
    "Say: The snow is white."
  ],
